;;; basw4-cx.scm -- C(X) as a unital Banach algebra (BA-SW3 finding F6), and the MAXIMAL IDEALS of
;;; C(X) (Remark 1.27 of the notes: they are exactly the sets M_x = {f : f(x) = 0}, x in X).
;;; F. J. Thayer, "Banach Algebras and Applications", ch. 1, Remark 1.27.  Agent BA-SW4, wave 2026-11-09.
;;; Destination: theorem-library/basw4-cx.scm.  Library: operator-algebras.  All proofs modulo 0.
;;; LOAD WINDOW: after theorem-library/basw3-urysohn (point-eval-injective, point-eval-val,
;;; rr-recip-lipschitz-ge-one), theorem-library/basw2-cx (the CCONT tower, read-offs and value laws),
;;; BA-SW's basw-top (bsw-compact-induction), BA-1's ba-spectrum (character-bounded).  No file cites this one.
;;; Helper prefix: bm4-.
;;;
;;; PART 1.  IS-UNITAL-BANACH-ALGEBRA(CCONT-ALGEBRA t) is FALSE as written: CCONT-ALGEBRA(t) is a
;;; 10-tuple and a generated IS-X pins the length of its instance (9 for a unital Banach algebra).  The
;;; unital Banach algebra of C(t) is the view UIBA-AS-UBA(CCONT-ALGEBRA t) (ccont-algebra-uba).  BA-1's
;;; general lemmas apply to it; the characters of the view are those of C(t) (ccont-characters-view; the
;;; general form for any unital involutive Banach algebra is uiba-characters-view), and
;;; character-bounded gives |chi(f)| <= ||f|| for every character of C(t) (ccont-character-bounded).
;;;
;;; PART 2.  The compactness argument of ccont-character-is-point-eval, stated for a subset bmi of C(t)
;;; with five closure laws (bm4-hyps: inside C(t), contains 0, closed under +, under scalars, under
;;; multiplication by C(t)) -- what a two-sided ideal gives (ccont-ideal-laws) and what ker(chi) satisfies:
;;; bump (c |g|^2 near a point where g in bmi does not vanish), cover (bsw-compact-induction), one
;;; (h >= 1 in bmi puts 1 in bmi), common-zero (without 1, all members vanish at one point).
;;;
;;; PART 3.  M_x is a proper two-sided ideal; it is maximal (an ideal J above M_x holding f with
;;; f(x) /= 0 holds (1/f(x))(f - (f - f(x) 1)) = 1); a maximal ideal I has a common zero x, so I is
;;; inside M_x, so I = M_x; hence ccont-maximal-ideals (t compact; no Hausdorff hypothesis), and
;;; ccont-point-ideal-injective (t Hausdorff: distinct points give distinct M_x, by point-eval-injective).
;;; ---- helpers (prefix bm4-) ----
(define (bm4-open?) (not (sequent-node-grounded? (proof-state-focus *ps*))))
(define (bm4-ass!) (if (and (bm4-open?) (dk-asm? (dk-goal))) (ass)))
(define (bm4-dump! tag)
  (display "\n*** DUMP ") (display tag) (newline)
  (for-each (lambda (l)
              (display "   GOAL: ") (display (expression->string (dk-goal-of l))) (newline)
              (for-each (lambda (a) (if (< (string-length (expression->string a)) 600) (begin (display "      asm: ") (display (expression->string a)) (newline))))
                        (dk-asms-of l)))
            (dk-open-leaves)))
(define (bm4-qed! name)
  (if (proof-done? *ps*)
      (begin (qed name) (topic! name 'analysis))
      (begin
        (display "\n*** basw4: ") (display name) (display " did NOT close.\n")
        (bm4-dump! name)
        (error "basw4: unfinished" name))))
